  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Ink Underline\n\nA hand-dragged ink stroke that draws itself across in a few stop-motion poses.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A hand-dragged ink underline belongs beneath a written headline, URL, or stat.\n- The scene already runs on the stop-motion clock and the stroke should arrive in the same discrete poses.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You are painting a highlight behind a word inside a sentence: use marker-highlight.\n- You want to circle or strike through something.\n\nVariables:\n- width (number, 100-1600): Width, default 420\n- color (color): Ink color, default \"#6f7f35\"\n- thickness (number, 2-40): Brush width, default 9\n- pressure (number, 0.05-1): Opening pressure, default 1\n- release (number, 0.05-1): Closing pressure, default 0.15\n- grain (number, 0-2): Grain, default 1\n- delay (number, 0-120): Delay, default 0\n- duration_steps (number, 2-10): Poses to draw, default 5\n- seed (string): Seed, default \"ink\"\n- step (number, 1-6): Frames per pose, default 3\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Ink Underline\n\n  A hand-dragged ink stroke that draws itself across in a few stop-motion poses.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/ink-underline/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"ink-underline\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"width\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Width\", \"description\": \"Stroke length in pixels (capped to 90% of the frame).\", \"default\": 420, \"min\": 100, \"max\": 1600, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Ink color\", \"description\": \"Color of the stroke.\", \"default\": \"#6f7f35\"},\n    {\"id\": \"thickness\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Brush width\", \"description\": \"Stroke thickness in pixels.\", \"default\": 9, \"min\": 2, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"pressure\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Opening pressure\", \"description\": \"Width at the start of the stroke, 0 to 1.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.05, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"release\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Closing pressure\", \"description\": \"Width at the end of the stroke, 0 to 1.\", \"default\": 0.15, \"min\": 0.05, \"max\": 1, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"grain\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Grain\", \"description\": \"How rough the brush edge is.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 2, \"step\": 0.05},\n    {\"id\": \"delay\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Delay\", \"description\": \"Frames before the stroke starts (30 fps).\", \"default\": 0, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"duration_steps\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Poses to draw\", \"description\": \"Stop-motion poses the stroke takes to draw.\", \"default\": 5, \"min\": 2, \"max\": 10, \"step\": 1},\n    {\"id\": \"seed\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Seed\", \"description\": \"Any text; changes the stroke wobble and grain.\", \"default\": \"ink\"},\n    {\"id\": \"step\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per pose\", \"description\": \"Stop-motion clock, in frames at 30 fps.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 6, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Ink Underline</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .iu-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .iu-box { position: relative; }\n        .iu-svg { position: absolute; display: block; overflow: visible; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"ink-underline\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"iu-clip\" class=\"iu-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"iu-box\" class=\"iu-box\">\n            <svg id=\"iu-svg\" class=\"iu-svg\">\n              <defs>\n                <filter id=\"iu-grain\" x=\"-30%\" y=\"-30%\" width=\"160%\" height=\"160%\">\n                  <feTurbulence id=\"iu-turb\" type=\"fractalNoise\" baseFrequency=\"0.7\" numOctaves=\"3\" seed=\"1\" result=\"brushGrain\" />\n                  <feDisplacementMap id=\"iu-disp\" in=\"SourceGraphic\" in2=\"brushGrain\" scale=\"0\" xChannelSelector=\"R\" yChannelSelector=\"G\" />\n                </filter>\n              </defs>\n              <path id=\"iu-path\" d=\"\" opacity=\"0.85\" />\n            </svg>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, options, fallback) {\n              return options.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function col(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            function fit(el, maxPx, size, ratio) {\n              // Shrink el's font size until its scrollWidth fits ratio of the frame width.\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var max = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * (ratio || 0.9));\n              if (el.scrollWidth > max) { size = Math.max(10, size * (max / el.scrollWidth)); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function ease(name, a, b, c, d) { return CustomEase.create(name, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\"); }\n            function mulberry32(a) { return function () { a |= 0; a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) | 0; var t = Math.imul(a ^ (a >>> 15), 1 | a); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; }; }\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            function ip(t, a, b, from, to, e) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : (t - a) / (b - a);\n              p = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p));\n              if (e) p = e(p);\n              return from + (to - from) * p;\n            }\n            function hash01(seed) {\n              var h = 2166136261;\n              for (var i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) { h ^= seed.charCodeAt(i); h = Math.imul(h, 16777619); }\n              h = Math.imul(h ^ (h >>> 13), 2246822519);\n              return ((h ^ (h >>> 16)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n            }\n            function hashRange(seed, lo, hi) { return lo + hash01(seed) * (hi - lo); }\n            // Snap a frame number down to a stop-motion pose.\n            function qf(frame, step) { return Math.floor(frame / step + 1e-6) * step; }\n            function kf(t, keys, vals, e) {\n              if (t <= keys[0]) return vals[0];\n              for (var i = 0; i < keys.length - 1; i++) if (t <= keys[i + 1]) return ip(t, keys[i], keys[i + 1], vals[i], vals[i + 1], e);\n              return vals[vals.length - 1];\n            }\n            // Per-frame drawing: a pure function of the timeline time, run from a tween's onUpdate.\n            function tick(draw) {\n              tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(tl.time()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n            var cubOut = ease(\"cub-out\", 0.215, 0.61, 0.355, 1);\n            var cubIn = ease(\"cub-in\", 0.55, 0.055, 0.675, 0.19);\n            var cubInOut = ease(\"cub-io\", 0.645, 0.045, 0.355, 1);\n\n            var box = document.getElementById(\"iu-box\");\n            var svg = document.getElementById(\"iu-svg\");\n            var pathEl = document.getElementById(\"iu-path\");\n            var width = Math.min(num(vars.width, 420, 100, 1600), root.clientWidth * 0.9);\n            var thick = num(vars.thickness, 9, 2, 40);\n            var pressure = num(vars.pressure, 1, 0.05, 1);\n            var release = num(vars.release, 0.15, 0.05, 1);\n            var grain = num(vars.grain, 1, 0, 2);\n            var delay = num(vars.delay, 0, 0, 120);\n            var poses = num(vars.duration_steps, 5, 2, 10);\n            var step = num(vars.step, 3, 1, 6);\n            var seed = str(vars.seed, \"ink\");\n            var grainScale = thick * 0.5 * grain;\n            var reach = thick / 2 + grainScale / 2;\n            var height = thick + 4;\n            box.style.width = width + \"px\"; box.style.height = height + \"px\";\n            svg.setAttribute(\"width\", width + reach * 2); svg.setAttribute(\"height\", height + reach * 2);\n            svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", -reach + \" \" + -reach + \" \" + (width + reach * 2) + \" \" + (height + reach * 2));\n            svg.style.left = -reach + \"px\"; svg.style.top = -reach + \"px\";\n            pathEl.setAttribute(\"fill\", col(vars.color, \"#6f7f35\"));\n            document.getElementById(\"iu-turb\").setAttribute(\"seed\", Math.floor(hash01(seed + \":grain\") * 1000));\n            document.getElementById(\"iu-disp\").setAttribute(\"scale\", grainScale);\n            if (grain > 0) pathEl.setAttribute(\"filter\", \"url(#iu-grain)\");\n            // Spine: a gentle cubic, sampled at 40 points.\n            var wob = hashRange(seed + \":w\", -1.2, 1.2), mid = thick / 2 + 2, N = 40, spine = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n              var u = i / (N - 1), v = 1 - u;\n              var c1x = width * 0.3, c2x = width * 0.7, c1y = mid + wob, c2y = mid - wob, ey = mid + wob * 0.6;\n              spine.push({ x: v * v * v * 2 + 3 * v * v * u * c1x + 3 * v * u * u * c2x + u * u * u * (width - 2), y: v * v * v * mid + 3 * v * v * u * c1y + 3 * v * u * u * c2y + u * u * u * ey });\n            }\n            function normal(k) {\n              var a = spine[k - 1] || spine[k], b = spine[k + 1] || spine[k];\n              var tx = b.x - a.x, ty = b.y - a.y, len = Math.hypot(tx, ty) || 1;\n              return { x: -ty / len, y: tx / len };\n            }\n            function curve(pts) {\n              var out = [];\n              for (var k = 0; k < pts.length - 1; k++) {\n                var p1 = pts[k], p0 = pts[k - 1] || p1, p2 = pts[k + 1], p3 = pts[k + 2] || p2;\n                out.push(\"C \" + (p1.x + (p2.x - p0.x) / 6) + \" \" + (p1.y + (p2.y - p0.y) / 6) + \", \" + (p2.x - (p3.x - p1.x) / 6) + \" \" + (p2.y - (p3.y - p1.y) / 6) + \", \" + p2.x + \" \" + p2.y);\n              }\n              return out.join(\" \");\n            }\n            function ribbon(progress) {\n              var drawn = Math.max(2, Math.round(progress * (spine.length - 1)) + 1), left = [], right = [];\n              for (var k = 0; k < drawn; k++) {\n                var half = (thick / 2) * (pressure + (release - pressure) * (k / (spine.length - 1)));\n                var n = normal(k);\n                left.push({ x: spine[k].x + n.x * half, y: spine[k].y + n.y * half });\n                right.push({ x: spine[k].x - n.x * half, y: spine[k].y - n.y * half });\n              }\n              var back = right.slice().reverse();\n              return \"M \" + left[0].x + \" \" + left[0].y + \" \" + curve(left) + \" L \" + back[0].x + \" \" + back[0].y + \" \" + curve(back) + \" Z\";\n            }\n            tick(function (t) {\n              var f = qf(Math.floor(t * 30 + 1e-6), step);\n              var progress = f <= delay ? 0 : f >= delay + poses * step ? 1 : (f - delay) / (poses * step);\n              box.style.opacity = progress > 0 ? 1 : 0;\n              pathEl.setAttribute(\"d\", ribbon(progress));\n            });\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"ink-underline\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
 "sha256": "f673af1f02d942b6a549f5662faa1399a70e5a68cb35ab9965c9e6c7c5364b1c",
